# Login

A signed-in session, CSRF-checked forms, a protected route that redirects an
anonymous visitor, and the POST/redirect/GET pattern throughout — every
piece from `docs/web.md`'s Sessions section, with a real (if tiny) user
table.

## Note

Real credentials never live in source; this is a demo with exactly one
account, `ada` / `correct horse`, checked in LOGOS rather than a database —
`docs/web.md`'s own PostgreSQL section is how a real app would look this up.

## To checkCredentials (username: Text) and (password: Text) -> Bool:
    If username is not equal to "ada":
        Return false.
    Return password is equal to "correct horse".

## Session
    a user, which is Text.

## Route GET / -> View:
    <main>
      <h1>Login demo</h1>
      {if the session's user is equal to "":}
        <p id="anonymous">Nobody is signed in. <a href="/login">Sign in</a></p>
      {else:}
        <p id="signed-in">Signed in as {the session's user}. <a href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a></p>
      {end}
    </main>

## Route GET /login -> View:
    <main>
      <h1>Sign in</h1>
      {if the session's user is not equal to "":}
        <p id="already">Already signed in as {the session's user}.</p>
      {end}
      <form method="post" action="/login">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value={csrf()}>
        <label>Username <input name="username"></label>
        <label>Password <input type="password" name="password"></label>
        <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
      </form>
    </main>

## Route POST /login (username: Text) and (password: Text) -> Response:
    If checkCredentials(username, password):
        Set the session's user to username.
        Return redirectTo("/dashboard").
    Return redirectTo("/login?failed=1").

## Route GET /dashboard -> Response:
    If the session's user is equal to "":
        Return redirectTo("/login").
    Return html("<main><h1>Welcome, " + the session's user + "</h1>" + "<form method=\"post\" action=\"/logout\"><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_csrf\" value=\"" + csrf() + "\"><button type=\"submit\">Sign out</button></form></main>").

## Route POST /logout -> Response:
    Set the session's user to "".
    Return redirectTo("/login").

## Main

Serve on port 8080.

## Test: the front page tells an anonymous visitor to sign in

Expect that route("GET", "/") contains "Nobody is signed in.".

## Test: the login form carries this visitor's own CSRF token

Expect that route("GET", "/login") contains "name=\"_csrf\"".

## Test: an anonymous visitor is redirected away from the dashboard

Expect that routeStatus("GET", "/dashboard") is equal to 302.
Expect that routeHeader("GET", "/dashboard", "location") is equal to "/login".

## Test: a login form with no CSRF token is refused before the route runs

Expect that routeStatus("POST", "/login") is equal to 403.

